==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, focus on going on multiple runs, collect many {{Tape|name=true}} as you can, and buy as many items as possible at [[Dandy's Shop]]. Going to {{CI|Dandy|name=true}} Runs is not recommended since the objective is the complete opposite.

==Strategies==
Teagan is a pretty versatile All-Rounded [[Toon]], but doesn't exactly focus on a certain niche as a result. She can be good for solo runs due to her impressive survivability, and also the fact that her playstyle can vary based on what you want. The only real issue is her 2 Star [[Stealth]], which may result in her taking away the [[Twisteds]] from a distractor and being encountered easily by them, meaning you'll have to be wary of your surroundings when playing as her.

Teagan's Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Teagan|name=true}}, makes her a great choice for inexperienced players or those who may end up dying more easily during runs. This Ability allows the player to heal themself at the cost of 75 {{Tape|name=true}}, which, during certain types of runs, won't be so hard to gather, though do note her longer Ability cool down, as it can hinder your survivability if you aren't aware of it.

Teagan can be a great protector thanks to their [[Stats]] and Ability, with the capability of guarding any teammates who are extracting and have equal or higher Stealth. They can also hover around teammates on 1 [[Heart]], bait ranged Twisted attacks to give distractors a head start, and escort slower teammates to the elevator during [[Panic Mode]]. They can easily take a hit for others, healing back up with her Ability.

Due to her Tape requiring Ability, players must gain as many Tapes as they can throughout the floors. As Tapes can be found everywhere on the map, mobility and exploration are key to using her effectively. It's important to note that {{II|Health Kit|name=true}}s and {{II|Bandage|name=false}}s are quite scarce in the first place, and by the time you reach around [[Floor]] 12+, you have a lot of Tapes that you have not spent, so asking teammates to let you pick up extra Tapes will help turn the excess into a very big help.

Other activities that produce Tapes are picking up Items, encountering each Twisted for the first time on the Floor, using her Ability (though it's not sustainable as a source), finishing [[Machines]], and surviving the Floor. Thus, it is recommended to pick up any Items that aren't valuable to your teammates if you have room in your inventory to immediately use them ({{II|Gumballs|name=false}}, {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false|plural=a}}, and {{II|Stealth Candy|name=false|plural=a}} being some of the least useful) and complete as many [[Machines]] as possible. Picking up {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false}}s is a great option, while buying a {{II|Valve|name=false}} from the pre-game shop and/or using {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} or {{TI|Wrench|name=true}} may be even more helpful. It is not recommended to go out of your way to encounter Twisteds, but waiting by the [[Elevator]] during [[Panic Mode]] and stepping out quickly once all of your teammates are safe to aggravate them and then getting back to safety can help get you the extra you need.

Whatsoever, having a {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} or {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} in your run might seem complicated, as both require even more Tapes to use their Active [[Abilities]]. Because Sprout and Ginger have to distribute heals out to a lot more people, allow them to pick up Tapes as you should get enough simply by doing tasks while playing the game. You can still obtain Tapes from encountering Twisteds, doing Machines or simply surviving the Floor. Infact, Teagan can even be somewhat helpful to healer Toons, as they have one less Toon to worry about (often) per individual Teagan. Teagan can still benefit from being healed by a healer if they are low on Tapes or on 1 Heart, but they overall have less of a need for it.

Teagan excels at doing Dandy Runs, as Health Kits and Bandages are already pretty rare to find on Floors. Since she benefits from Tapes in a run that makes them useless, ask your teammates to leave all Tapes for her to pick up unless Sprout or Ginger are also present, as their Abilities also rely on Tapes.

Teagan is a decent choice for completing [[Dyle's Floor]], as even though their extraction Stats are average, they are by no means terrible. Her above average Stamina can make her quite efficient on Treadmill Machines, and the Stealth can help with saving teammates. Do note that while her Ability can help with the relatively large amount of Twisteds, it’s ineffective against {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} due to his insta-kill. With the abundance of Machines, tape income will be high, and the +50 Stamina gained will make your survivability even more potent, even if it may be somewhat unnecessary on earlier Floors with the already above average Stamina. 

Unless you are in a solo run, it is not recommended to take any Health Kits or Bandages as they are better left for your teammates due to Teagan's ability to heal herself. However, if you are low on health and Tapes, you can still take one.

